# Fast Edit Skill

Use this rule for small, low-risk edits.

## Good use cases

Use for:

- removing text
- renaming variables
- adding type hints
- updating docstrings
- simplifying small functions
- adjusting labels
- changing tooltips
- generating small tests
- converting simple config classes to dataclasses

## Rules

- Keep changes minimal.
- Preserve existing behavior.
- Touch the fewest files possible.
- Prefer existing helpers and patterns.
- Do not redesign architecture.
- Do not perform broad refactors.
- Do not modify unrelated code.
- Explain only what changed.

## Do not

- Do not add new dependencies.
- Do not create new helper systems unless requested.
- Do not rename public APIs unless requested.
- Do not change formatting across unrelated files.
- Do not run the full test suite for a tiny edit unless requested.
- Do not combine cleanup with behavior changes.

## Checklist

Before finishing:

- Confirm the requested edit was made.
- Confirm unrelated files were not changed.
- Mention the targeted test that should be run.
- Run or suggest the smallest relevant test.
- Mention if no test was run.
- Check linting only when the touched area normally requires it.